               <msContents>
                  <summary>Anonymous commentary on prayers, with additional quoted
                     commentaries</summary>
                  <msItem>
                     <title type="desc" key="work_3376">Commentary on Prayers</title>
                     <title type="desc" xml:lang="he" key="work_3376">פרוש התפלות</title>
                     <title type="desc" xml:lang="he-Latn-x-lc">Perush ha-tefillot</title>
                     <textLang mainLang="he">Hebrew</textLang>
                     <note>This commentary by an anonymous author contains quoted sections of other
                        commentaries, including those by <persName key="person_59876084">Joseph
                           Kara</persName> (<locus>ff. 101r-111r, 114r-142v</locus>; probably also
                           <locus>ff. 168r-180v, 206v-233v</locus>), <persName key="person_75197037"
                           >Eliezer ben Nathan of Mainz</persName> (on the New Year liturgy;
                           <locus>ff. 111r-114r</locus>), <persName key="person_19684048"
                           >Rashi</persName> (on <hi rend="italic">piyyutim</hi>; <locus>ff.
                           114v-160r</locus>). <locus>Ff. 206v-233v</locus> also incorporates
                        additions by <persName key="person_308257340">Solomon b.
                        Samson</persName>.</note>
                     <note>The names of many other authors are quoted; these include <persName
                           key="person_1085">Joseph ben Samuel Tov-ʿElem (Bonfils)</persName>,
                           <persName key="person_150">Samuel ben Barukh of Bamberg</persName>,
                           <persName key="person_7081">David ben Sheʾaltiel</persName>, <persName
                           key="person_301948260">Eleazar ben Judah of Worms</persName>, <persName
                           key="person_1077">Benjamin of Canterbury</persName>, <persName
                           key="person_20145304381978571579">Jacob Nazir</persName>, <persName
                           key="person_22494885">Ephraim ben Jacob of Bonn</persName>, <persName
                           key="person_33403361">Meir ben Isaac Sheliʼaḥ Ẓibbur</persName>,
                           <persName key="person_7082">Meir of Lisieux</persName>, and <persName
                           key="person_7083">Ḳalonymus ben Yehudah</persName>.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
