                  <handDesc>
                     <summary>Ashkenazic semi-cursive script.</summary>
                     <handNote> Copied by four hands. First hand: <locus from="1v" to="105r">ff.
                           1v-105r, col. 2, 1. 1</locus>, and <locus from="161r" to="249v"
                           >161r-249v</locus>. Second hand: <locus from="105r" to="133v">ff. 105r,
                           col. 2, 1. 2-133v</locus>, <locus from="143r" to="150v">ff.
                           143r-150v</locus>, and <locus from="250r" to="270v">ff.
                        250r-270v</locus>. Third hand: <locus from="134r" to="142v">ff.
                           134r-142v</locus>, and <locus from="151r" to="160r">ff.
                        151r-160r</locus>. Fourth hand (possibly later):<locus from="271" to="278"
                           >last quire (ff. 271-278)</locus>. </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
                  <bindingDesc>
                     <p>Dark brown leather with rough, pronounced grain over paper boards;
                        blind-tooled decorations on both upper and lower boards. On the spine, a
                        damaged paper slip bearing the printed number 10[...]3; the number 170 has
                        been painted in white.</p>
                     <condition>The leather covering the boards have been damaged in many places and
                        have been repaired using dark brown leather with finer grain. Two clasps now
                        missing. Many wormholes on the leather covering ther lower board: these are
                        found also on the final folios but not on the inner side of the lower board,
                        indicating that this was a later replacement.</condition>
                  </bindingDesc>
